<h2>3. Swagger OpenAPI UI Integration Details</h2>
<p>In the Swagger UI (served at <code>/api/docs</code>), the NestJS OpenAPI decorator conventions were enhanced to deliver maximum clarity:</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Summary Tags:</strong> The <code>summary</code> property of <code>@ApiOperation</code> ends with a clear bracketed role tag (e.g. <code>[Roles: MEMBER, OWNER, ADMIN]</code>). Because Swagger UI displays the summary directly on collapsed accordion headers, developers and auditors immediately see permission levels without clicking.</li>
  <li><strong>Markdown Description:</strong> Expanding each endpoint presents a structured breakdown:
    <ul>
      <li><code>**Route:** METHOD /path</code> &mdash; Exact HTTP method and route path.</li>
      <li><code>**Purpose:** ...</code> &mdash; Clear business logic explanation.</li>
      <li><code>**Allowed Roles:** ...</code> &mdash; Enumerated list of authorized roles.</li>
      <li><code>**Permissions:** ...</code> &mdash; Contextual permissions, ownership constraints, or author isolation rules.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Global RBAC Matrix in Document Header:</strong> The OpenAPI root documentation description rendered at the top of <code>/api/docs</code> contains a dedicated Role-Based Access Control table and authentication instructions for Bearer JWT and Cookie Auth.</li>
</ol>

